$.\n\nNow $S = S_1 + S_2 = \\sum_{k=1}^\\infty 2^{2k - k^2} - \\sum_{k=1}^\\infty 2^{-k^2} + 1 - \\sum_{k=1}^\\infty 2^{-k^2}$\n\n$= 1 + \\sum_{k=1}^\\infty 2^{2k - k^2} - 2\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty 2^{-k^2}$.\n\nNote that $2^{2k - k^2} = 2^{-(k^2 - 2k)} = 2^{-(k-1)^2 + 1} = 2 \\cdot 2^{-(k-1)^2}$.\n\nSo $\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty 2^{2k - k^2} = 2\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty 2^{-(k-1)^2} = 2\\sum_{j=0}^\\infty 2^{-j^2} = 2(2^0 + \\sum_{j=1}^\\infty 2^{-j^2}) = 2(1 + \\sum_{j=1}^\\infty 2^{-j^2})$.\n\nSo $S = 1 + 2(1 + \\sum_{j=1}^\\infty 2^{-j^2}) - 2\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty 2^{-k^2} = 1 + 2 + 2\\sum_{j=1}^\\infty 2^{-j^2} - 2\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty 2^{-k^2} = 3$.\n\nWait, that's beautiful! The sums cancel and we get $S = 3$.\n\nLet me double-check. $S = 1 + 2(1 + \\sum_{j=1}^\\infty 2^{-j^2}) - 2\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty 2^{-k^2} = 1 + 2 + 2\\sum - 2\\sum = 3$.\n\nSo $S = 3$.\n\nLet me verify numerically with a few terms.\n\n$n=1$: $f(1) = \\lfloor 1.5 \\rfloor = 1$. Term: $(2^1 + 2^{-1})/2^1 = (2 + 0.5)/2 = 1.25$.\n$n=2$: $f(2) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{2}+0.5 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1.914 \\rfloor = 1$. Term: $(2+0.5)/4 = 0.625$.\n$n=3$: $f(3) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{3}+0.5 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.232 \\rfloor = 2$. Term: $(4+0.25)/8 = 0.53125$.\n$n=4$: $f(4) = \\lfloor 2.5 \\rfloor = 2$. Term: $(4+0.25)/16 = 0.265625$.\n$n=5$: $f(5) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{5}+0.5 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.736 \\rfloor = 2$. Term: $(4+0.25)/32 = 0.1328125$.\n$n=6$: $f(6) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{6}+0.5 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.949 \\rfloor = 2$. Term: $(4+0.25)/64 = 0.06640625$.\n\nSum so far: 1.25 + 0.625 + 0.53125 + 0.265625 + 0.1328125 + 0.06640625 = 2.87109375.\n\n$n=7$: $f(7) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{7}+0.5 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.146 \\rfloor = 3$. Term: $(8+0.125)/128 = 0.0634765625$.\n$n=8$: $f(8) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{8}+0.5 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.328 \\rfloor = 3$. Term: $(8.125)/256 = 0.03173828125$.\n$n=9$: $f(9) = \\lfloor 3.5 \\rfloor = 3$. Term: $8.125/512 = 0.015869140625$.\n$n=10$: $f(10) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{10}+0.5 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.662 \\rfloor = 3$. Term: $8.125/1024 = 0.0079345703125$.\n$n=11$: $f(11) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{11}+0.5 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.817 \\rfloor = 3$. Term: $8.125/2048 = 0.00396728515625$.\n$n=12$: $f(12) = \\lfloor \\sqrt{12}+0.5 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.964 \\rfloor = 3$. Term: $8.125/4096 = 0.001983642578125$.\n\nAdding n=7 through 12: 0.0634765625 + 0.03173828125 + 0.015869140625 + 0.0079345703125 + 0.00396728515625 + 0.001983642578125 = 0.124969482421875.\n\nTotal so far: 2.87109375 + 0.124969482421875 = 2.996063232421875.\n\nGetting close to 3. The remaining terms will add up to about 0.0039... Yes, this confirms $S = 3$.\n\nThe answer is $\\boxed{3}$.\n\nNow let me write up the proof properly.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1787232271}
